[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done. [38;5;153mindex.html[39m now has a single checkbox with a label in [38;5;153m<main>[39m, plus a CSS rule that strikes through and greys the
  text when checked.

  - No JavaScript — the browser owns the on/off state.
  - Wrapping the input in [38;5;153m<label>[39m makes the text itself clickable to toggle.
  - The [38;5;153m:checked + span[39m sibling selector is why the text is wrapped in a [38;5;153m<span>[39m.

  Not verified in a browser — I didn't open the page. The repo has no test setup, so if you want confirmation beyond
  reading the markup, opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m is the check.

